  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "The JS/TS Packs name only the member of a member call, never its receiver, so Bun.serve, Bun.spawn, Bun.file and Bun.write are matched by member name alone and any same-named method call in the project matches with them.",
      "Bun.serve's handler table -- fetch, websocket, error -- is an object literal property whose value is an identifier. omega-typescript emits no fact for an object literal property and the call.method span covers only the member name, so no join reaches it; which function answers a request is not stated.",
      "Bun.env and process.env are member references, not calls, and no JS/TS Pack emits a fact for a bare member reference, so which environment variables a Bun project reads cannot be answered.",
      "Argument values -- ports, file paths, SQL text, test titles, bunfig.toml setting values -- are published as fields by no Pack, so a site is addressed by its position and named by its API rather than by what it operates on."
    ]
  },
